README.md (lines 1-106 of 106)
   1 | # Protein Binder Design Benchmark
   2 | 
   3 | SkyDiscover benchmark for evolving Proteina-Complexa binder-design run
   4 | specifications against RCSB 3DI3 chain B, human IL-7Ralpha ectodomain.
   5 | 
   6 | The evolved program does not run models directly. It returns a constrained
   7 | dictionary of hotspots, binder length, sampling settings, and test-time search
   8 | settings. `evaluator.py` validates that dictionary, launches Proteina-Complexa
   9 | generation, reads Proteina's `rewards_*.csv`, and reports `combined_score`.
  10 | 
  11 | ## Files
  12 | 
  13 | - `initial_program.py`: seed EVOLVE-BLOCK returning a Proteina run spec.
  14 | - `evaluator.py`: SkyDiscover evaluator with `evaluate`, `evaluate_stage1`,
  15 |   and `evaluate_stage2`.
  16 | - `config.yaml`: LLM prompt and cascade evaluator settings.
  17 | - `prepare_3di3_assets.py`: reproducible RCSB download and target extraction.
  18 | - `assets/3di3.pdb`: raw RCSB PDB coordinates.
  19 | - `assets/3di3.cif`: raw RCSB mmCIF coordinates.
  20 | - `assets/3di3_chain_b_il7ra_target.pdb`: chain-B-only Proteina target PDB.
  21 | - `assets/target_metadata.json`: allowed hotspots and interface candidates.
  22 | 
  23 | ## Target
  24 | 
  25 | The benchmark targets IL-7Ralpha, chain B of 3DI3. The seed uses the
  26 | RFdiffusion/OpenProtein prior hotspots `B62`, `B84`, and `B143`, but the LLM is
  27 | expected to choose hotspots as part of the optimization problem. The evaluator
  28 | accepts any modeled chain-B residue listed in `assets/target_metadata.json`.
  29 | 
  30 | The cleaned target PDB strips chain A and glycan chains C-E so Proteina sees a
  31 | standard protein target. The raw coordinate files remain in `assets/` for
  32 | reproducibility.
  33 | 
  34 | ## Environment
  35 | 
  36 | The evaluator expects Proteina-Complexa at the sibling directory
  37 | `../Proteina-Complexa` relative to the `skydiscover/` checkout (that is,
  38 | `protein-ag/Proteina-Complexa` when both repos live in the same workspace).
  39 | 
  40 | Override with:
  41 | 
  42 | ```bash
  43 | export PROTEINA_COMPLEXA_ROOT=/path/to/Proteina-Complexa
  44 | ```
  45 | 
  46 | Required for real model evaluations:
  47 | 
  48 | ```bash
  49 | export CKPT_PATH=/path/to/complexa/checkpoints
  50 | export AF2_DIR=/path/to/alphafold/params
  51 | ```
  52 | 
  53 | `CKPT_PATH` should contain `complexa.ckpt` and `complexa_ae.ckpt`. The default
  54 | seed uses `checkpoint_selection: "complexa_default"`, which maps to
  55 | `complexa.ckpt`.
  56 | 
  57 | For schema-only smoke tests that do not run Proteina:
  58 | 
  59 | ```bash
  60 | export SKYDISCOVER_BINDER_VALIDATE_ONLY=1
  61 | ```
  62 | 
  63 | ## Run
  64 | 
  65 | From the SkyDiscover repo:
  66 | 
  67 | ```bash
  68 | uv run skydiscover-run \
  69 |   benchmarks/protein_binder_design/initial_program.py \
  70 |   benchmarks/protein_binder_design/evaluator.py \
  71 |   -c benchmarks/protein_binder_design/config.yaml \
  72 |   -s adaevolve \
  73 |   -i 20
  74 | ```
  75 | 
  76 | Local evaluator smoke test:
  77 | 
  78 | ```bash
  79 | SKYDISCOVER_BINDER_VALIDATE_ONLY=1 \
  80 | python benchmarks/protein_binder_design/evaluator.py \
  81 |   benchmarks/protein_binder_design/initial_program.py
  82 | ```
  83 | 
  84 | Regenerate target assets:
  85 | 
  86 | ```bash
  87 | python benchmarks/protein_binder_design/prepare_3di3_assets.py
  88 | ```
  89 | 
  90 | ## Scoring
  91 | 
  92 | `evaluator.py` runs Proteina's `search_binder_local_pipeline` with Hydra
  93 | overrides for the benchmark target and evolved hyperparameters. It reads the
  94 | latest `rewards_*.csv` and scores finite `total_reward` values.
  95 | 
  96 | Returned metrics include:
  97 | 
  98 | - `combined_score`: bounded SkyDiscover objective, higher is better.
  99 | - `best_total_reward`: best Proteina generation reward.
 100 | - `mean_total_reward`: mean finite Proteina generation reward.
 101 | - `num_valid_designs`: number of generated designs with finite reward.
 102 | - `selected_hotspots`: hotspot residues chosen by the candidate.
 103 | - `search_algorithm`: Proteina test-time search strategy.
 104 | 
 105 | Cascade evaluation uses a smaller Stage 1 run to reject invalid or weak
 106 | candidates before Stage 2 performs the fuller bounded run.
